# Duffel flight-search API (https://duffel.com).
# Sign up (free), then Dashboard → Developers → Access tokens → create one.
# Test tokens start with "duffel_test_"; live tokens with "duffel_live_".
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and paste your token (NEVER commit .env.local).
# In Vercel, set it under Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# Without a token, /api/search returns a "connect the API" state — it never
# fabricates flights.
#
# NOTE: TEST tokens mostly return the fictional "Duffel Airways", which maps to
# no real loyalty program (so searches show "no fundable options"). Use a LIVE
# token to see real carriers and the full points-vs-cash ranking.

DUFFEL_ACCESS_TOKEN=
